From feaa74a93829471d7888e50bbdaf7bf759febb7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:15:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Native: touch on the shops and the Pause menu

include/arena/arena_touch.h: helpers that turn a tap on a window's grid of
choices into what the keys do. A tap on another choice moves the
selection there; a tap on the selected one presses A for that frame, so
the screen's own A code runs unchanged. Cells are placed from the
window's interior, as its sprites and cursor are; Touch_TappedUiCell
widens cells smaller than the 24-pixel minimum at the grid's edges.

Taps now work on the shops' stock row (with its page arrows), party row
and bag grid (buying, selling, the item picker), the arena's shops and
member choosers, and the Pause menu, beside the icon rows from patch 51.
In the SDL build the right mouse button is B, so a mouse alone can back
out.

The GBA ROM is byte-identical.

